---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import { book, href, renderContent } from '../lib/book';
---
<Shell title="About this edition"><main id="main" class="site-width"><header class="page-intro" id="top"><span class="eyebrow">SCOPE, CONTRIBUTION, AND EVIDENCE</span><h1>About this edition.</h1><p>A technical monograph on the complete agentic system, reviewed through 29 October 2026.</p></header><div class="about-copy"><section id="authorship" class="author-credit"><span class="eyebrow">AUTHOR</span><h2 data-author-credit>{book.metadata.author}</h2></section><h2>The complete publication</h2><p>This online edition preserves all 34 chapters, 266 sections, 39 subsections, 37 tables, 35 illustrations, and 356 cited references from the accepted manuscript. Equations, figure numbers, and citations retain the identifiers used in the PDF.</p><p><a href={href('downloads/agentic-state.pdf')}>Read the complete PDF</a> or <a href={href('downloads/agentic-state-source.zip')}>download the modular LaTeX source</a>. The PDF contains 482 main-text pages, excluding its front matter and references.</p><h2>The argument and its limits</h2><div class="prose" set:html={renderContent(book.metadata.frontMatterHtml.replace(/<(\/?)h1\b/g, '<$1h3'))}></div><h2>Inspect the evidence</h2><p>The <a href={href('downloads/source-crosswalk.csv')}>source crosswalk</a> retains versions and review limits. The <a href={href('downloads/validation.json')}>validation record</a> describes the performed checks and their scope. Source inspection is not experimental reproduction; this edition reports no new experimental measurements.</p><h2>Online edition</h2><p>This interface is independently implemented with Astro and TypeScript. It uses self-hosted ET Book and Inter fonts, Phosphor interface icons, and KaTeX mathematics. Scientific illustrations and the original editorial artwork were generated with an image-generation tool; the tool did not expose its exact model identifier.</p><p>Design references informed the editorial direction. This site does not reuse the previous book’s UI code or its scientific content. The monograph remains the source of truth for this edition.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/neuralatlasai/AutonomyAtlas">Repository, source, and issue tracker</a> · <a href={href('licenses/')}>Third-party licenses</a></p></div></main></Shell>
